+ * KeInitializeInterrupt registration (vector 1, Interrupt object
+ * 0x00DFB3C0, ServiceContext 0x800008C4), and its KeInsertQueueDpc call
+ * (confirmed via the icall slot at 0x4E3CBC resolving to kernel ordinal
+ * 119) were identified. Real hardware fires this asynchronously via IRQ;
+ * this project has no interrupt-line model, so it is synthesized instead,
+ * from a point that is already proven safe for host-to-guest calls
+ * (compare xbox_bridge_drain_guest_dpcs below, and
+ * nfl2k5_gpu_notify_service in recomp_manual.c) -- never from an unrelated
+ * host thread, which would run the guest call on that thread's own,
+ * uninitialized TLS register context.
